    "call_sid": "CAxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
    "account_sid": "ACxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
    "reason": "callended"
  }
}

`reason`: `stopped` (applet ended) · `callended` (caller hung up)

Events — your server → Exotel _(VoiceBot Applet only)_

{
  "event": "media",
  "sequence_number": 3,
  "stream_sid": "",
  "media": {
    "chunk": 2,
    "timestamp": "10",
    "payload": ""
  }
}

DTMF (Bidirectional only)

Key press events from the caller.

{
  "event": "dtmf",
  "sequence_number": 1,
  "stream_sid": "",
  "dtmf": {
    "duration": "200",
    "digit": "5"
  }
}

Stop

Sent when the stream ends.

{
  "event": "stop",
  "sequence_number": 10,
  "stream_sid": "",
  "stop": {
    "call_sid": "",
    "account_sid": "",
    "reason": "stopped"
  }
}

`reason` values: `stopped` (applet ended) or `callended` (caller hung up).

Mark

Notification that a previously sent audio chunk has finished playing.

{
  "event": "mark",
  "sequence_number": 15,
  "stream_sid": "",
  "mark": {
    "name": ""
  }
}

Messages TO Exotel (Outgoing — Bidirectional Only)

Media

Send audio back to the caller (same format as incoming).

{
  "event": "media",
  "stream_sid": "",
  "media": {
    "payload": ""
  }
}

Mark

Request a notification when your audio finishes playing.

{
  "event": "mark",
  "stream_sid": "",
  "mark": {
    "name": "my-label"
  }
}

Clear

Remove all queued (unplayed) audio from the buffer. Useful for interrupting bot responses when the user speaks.

{
  "event": "clear",
  "stream_sid": ""
}

:::tip
Send audio in smaller chunks for more responsive Clear behavior — the Clear command only removes audio that hasn't started playing yet.
:::

Event Field Reference

// Express server handling Passthru requests
app.post('/exotel/passthru', (req, res) => {
  const callerNumber = req.body.CallFrom;
  const callSid = req.body.CallSid;

  // Look up caller in your database
  const customer = db.findByPhone(callerNumber);

  if (customer && customer.isVIP) {
    // Route to VIP flow
    res.status(200).send('https://my.exotel.com/exoml/start/vip-flow');
  } else {
    // Route to standard flow
    res.status(200).send('https://my.exotel.com/exoml/start/standard-flow');
  }
});

Server Requirements

| Requirement | Details |
|------------|---------|
| HTTPS | Your endpoint must support HTTPS (TLS 1.2+) |
| Response time | Must respond within the configured timeout (default 15 seconds) |
| HTTP status | Return 200 for success; 4xx/5xx triggers the error path |
| Availability | Must be publicly accessible from Exotel's servers |
| Content-Type | Return `text/plain` or `application/json` |

